      level: "Challenge",
      question: "Sales Summary Analyzer",
      hindiDescription: "### Problem Statement\nUser se space-separated `Item:Sales` records input lein (e.g. `Pen:50 Book:200 Pen:30 Book:50 Bag:300`).\nDictionary me item-wise total sales aggregate karein.\nPehli line par aggregated dictionary print karein.\nDusri line par highest-selling product `{Item}: {Total}` print karein (ties broken alphabetically).\n\n### Instructions\n- Parse and accumulate sales into dict.\n- Print dictionary.\n- Find max sales and print `{item}: {sales}`.\n\n### Progressive Hints\n1. Accumulate totals in `totals[item] = totals.get(item, 0) + sales`.\n2. Print dict.\n3. Find and print top seller.",
      referenceCode: "records = input().split()\ntotals = {}\nfor r in records:\n    item, s_str = r.split(':')\n    totals[item] = totals.get(item, 0) + int(s_str)\nprint(totals)\ntop = min(totals.items(), key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0]))\nprint(f'{top[0]}: {top[1]}')",
