      question: "Employee Department Analyzer",
      hindiDescription: "### Problem Statement\nUser se space-separated `Dept:EmpId` records input lein (e.g. `IT:101 HR:102 IT:103 IT:101 HR:104`).\nHar department ke unique employee count calculate karein (dict of sets use karke) aur department names ke sorted order me `{Dept}: {Count}` print karein.\n\n### Instructions\n- `dept_map = {}`\n- `for r in records: d, emp = r.split(':'); dept_map.setdefault(d, set()).add(emp)`\n- For each sorted dept, print `{d}: {len(dept_map[d])}`.\n\n### Progressive Hints\n1. Group unique employee IDs in sets by department.\n2. Sort departments alphabetically.\n3. Print `{dept}: {count}`.",
      referenceCode: "records = input().split()\ndept_map = {}\nfor r in records:\n    d, emp = r.split(':')\n    dept_map.setdefault(d, set()).add(emp)\nfor d in sorted(dept_map.keys()):\n    print(f'{d}: {len(dept_map[d])}')",
