      "level": "Mastery",
      "question": "Cooperative super() Basics",
      "hindiDescription": "### Problem Statement\nMultiple inheritance me cooperative `super().__init__()` chain demonstrate karein.\n\n### Instructions\n- Classes `A`, `B(A)`, `C(A)`, `D(B, C)` me cooperative init.\n- Instance create karke order trace print karein.\n\n### Progressive Hints\n1. Har level par `super().__init__()` call karein.\n2. Trace logs append karein.\n3. Output verify karein.",
      "referenceCode": "class Base:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.steps = ['Base']\n\nclass Left(Base):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.steps.append('Left')\n\nclass Right(Base):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.steps.append('Right')\n\nclass Combined(Left, Right):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.steps.append('Combined')\n\nc = Combined()\nprint('Init steps:', c.steps)",
      "starterCode": "# Cooperative super() Basics\n",
