      "id": "OOP-11-05",
      "number": 5,
      "level": "Practice",
      "question": "Multiple Abstract Methods",
      "hindiDescription": "### Problem Statement\nAbstract class `Vehicle(ABC)` me do abstract methods `start()` aur `stop()` require karein aur `Bike` me dono implement karein.\n\n### Instructions\n- Dono methods implement karein.\n- Test calls print karein.\n\n### Progressive Hints\n1. Dono abstract methods par decorator lagayein.\n2. Child me dono override karein.\n3. Test and print.",
      "referenceCode": "from abc import ABC, abstractmethod\n\nclass Vehicle(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    def start(self): pass\n    @abstractmethod\n    def stop(self): pass\n\nclass Bike(Vehicle):\n    def start(self): return 'Bike started'\n    def stop(self): return 'Bike stopped'\n\nb = Bike()\nprint(f'{b.start()} | {b.stop()}')",
      "starterCode": "# Multiple Abstract Methods\n",
