      "number": 8,
      "level": "Apply",
      "question": "Abstract Employee Class",
      "hindiDescription": "### Problem Statement\nAbstract `Employee(ABC)` me required `calculate_pay()` method ho. `SalariedEmployee` aur `HourlyEmployee` implement karein.\n\n### Instructions\n- Salaried: 50000\n- Hourly: 40 hrs * 500/hr = 20000\n- Print calculated pays.\n\n### Progressive Hints\n1. Enforce pay calculation contract.\n2. Implement different pay models.\n3. Display results.",
      "referenceCode": "from abc import ABC, abstractmethod\n\nclass Employee(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    def calculate_pay(self): pass\n\nclass Salaried(Employee):\n    def __init__(self, sal): self.sal = sal\n    def calculate_pay(self): return self.sal\n\nclass Hourly(Employee):\n    def __init__(self, hrs, rate): self.hrs, self.rate = hrs, rate\n    def calculate_pay(self): return self.hrs * self.rate\n\nprint(f'Salaried: Rs.{Salaried(50000).calculate_pay()} | Hourly: Rs.{Hourly(40, 500).calculate_pay()}')",
      "starterCode": "# Abstract Employee Class\n",
