      "question": "Final Capstone: OOP Data Management System",
      "hindiDescription": "### Problem Statement\nBuild a complete OOP system:\n- Abstract `BaseRecord(ABC)` with property `id` and abstract `summary()`\n- `StudentRecord` and `EmployeeRecord` inheriting from it\n- `RecordManager` class supporting Add, List and Count\n- Full polymorphic summary output print karein.\n\n### Instructions\n- Student: 'S-101: Rahul (Marks 92)'\n- Employee: 'E-201: Priya (Salary 60000)'\n- Manager counts and prints all records.\n\n### Progressive Hints\n1. Combine Inheritance, Abstraction, Polymorphism and Properties.\n2. RecordManager stores collection.\n3. Print comprehensive report.",
      "referenceCode": "from abc import ABC, abstractmethod\n\nclass BaseRecord(ABC):\n    def __init__(self, rec_id):\n        self._id = rec_id\n    @property\n    def id(self): return self._id\n    @abstractmethod\n    def summary(self): pass\n\nclass StudentRecord(BaseRecord):\n    def __init__(self, rec_id, name, marks):\n        super().__init__(rec_id)\n        self.name, self.marks = name, marks\n    def summary(self):\n        return f'{self.id}: {self.name} (Marks {self.marks})'\n\nclass EmployeeRecord(BaseRecord):\n    def __init__(self, rec_id, name, salary):\n        super().__init__(rec_id)\n        self.name, self.salary = name, salary\n    def summary(self):\n        return f'{self.id}: {self.name} (Salary Rs.{self.salary})'\n\nclass RecordManager:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.records = []\n    def add(self, r):\n        self.records.append(r)\n    def report(self):\n        return [r.summary() for r in self.records]\n\nmgr = RecordManager()\nmgr.add(StudentRecord('S-101', 'Rahul', 92))\nmgr.add(EmployeeRecord('E-201', 'Priya', 60000))\nfor line in mgr.report():\n    print(line)",
