      number: 10,
      level: "Challenge",
      question: "return Statement Challenge",
      hindiDescription: "### Problem Statement\nFunction `evaluate_result(marks, max_marks)` banayein.\nAgar `max_marks <= 0` ya `marks < 0` ya `marks > max_marks` hai to return karein `'Invalid Input'`.\nWarna percentage calculate karein, 40% par pass status check karein aur format `<pct:.1f>% - <Pass/Fail>` return karein.\nUser se space-separated marks aur max_marks input lekar result print karein.\n\n### Instructions\n- Input validation, percentage calculation, and formatted return.\n\n### Progressive Hints\n1. Validate bounds.\n2. Calculate percentage: `(marks / max_marks) * 100`.\n3. Return formatted result.",
      referenceCode: "def evaluate_result(marks, max_marks):\n    if max_marks <= 0 or marks < 0 or marks > max_marks:\n        return 'Invalid Input'\n    pct = (marks / max_marks) * 100\n    status = 'Pass' if pct >= 40 else 'Fail'\n    return f'{pct:.1f}% - {status}'\n\nm, mx = map(int, input().split())\nprint(evaluate_result(m, mx))",
